Defects found:

- **NEGATION DROPPED, line 39.** Exact input: `bag(NUM, "effect -0.1234")` and `bag(NUM, "effect 0.1234")` both yield `Counter({"0.1234": 1})`. Consequence: a sign reversal is invisible to the estimate invariant.

- **SELECTOR KEYED TO WRONG FORM, line 66.** Exact input: `panel_raw('<section id="pn-paper"><h2>Paper</h2><p>A</p></section><section class=\'panel\'><p>0.9999</p></section>')`. Consequence: the Paper panel boundary is missed for single-quoted `class='panel'`, so non-Paper bytes are included.

- **SELECTOR KEYED TO WRONG FORM, line 108.** Exact input: `flow_paths('<div id="pn-paper"><h2>Paper</h2><div class="prov-block"><small>&larr; results.by_outcome.x</small></div><div class="panel"></div>')`. Consequence: double-quoted provenance blocks are not removed, so provenance markers are counted as sentence-flow field paths.

- **INSTRUMENT READS DIFFERENT COPY THAN CLAIMED, line 171.** Exact input: before `'<div data-nct="NCT12345678"></div>'`, after `'<div></div>'`. Consequence: an invisible attribute value is reported as a lost rendered registration ID.

- **CHECK CANNOT FAIL, line 140.** Exact command: `python scripts/prove_register_change_moved_no_content.py before.html after.html --content-change obj.json`, with `obj.json` containing `{"outcomes":[{"name":"Primary outcome mortality"}]}`. Consequence: the object is silently skipped because only `sys.argv[3]` is considered, disabling the registered-outcome check.

- **SELECTOR TRUNCATES THE EVIDENCE, line 185.** Exact input: object name `"123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890LOST"`, before contains that full string, after contains only the first 60 characters. Consequence: loss of the registered outcome suffix is accepted as unchanged.

No proven hit for CRLF text comparison, merged-cell tabulation, zero-vs-absent, or wrapper-status reporting from this file alone.
